Two separate issues:

**1. `StaticResource` vs `DynamicResource`**

`StaticResource` resolves once at XAML load time and never updates. Switch to `DynamicResource` for any value that can change at runtime:

```xml
<!-- Won't update at runtime -->
<Label TextColor="{StaticResource PrimaryTextColor}" />

<!-- Will update when the resource dictionary changes -->
<Label TextColor="{DynamicResource PrimaryTextColor}" />
```

Then swap themes by merging/replacing the dictionary:

```csharp
var mergedDictionaries = Application.Current.Resources.MergedDictionaries;
mergedDictionaries.Clear();
mergedDictionaries.Add(useDark ? new DarkTheme() : new LightTheme());
```

**2. Activity restarting on system theme change**

Android destroys and recreates the `Activity` on `uiMode` configuration changes. Prevent this by adding to your `MainActivity.cs`:

```csharp
[Activity(
    ConfigurationChanges = ConfigChanges.UiMode | ConfigChanges.Orientation | ConfigChanges.ScreenSize)]
public class MainActivity : MauiAppCompatActivity { }
```

This tells Android your app handles the theme change itself. Then detect the system change:

```csharp
public override void OnConfigurationChanged(Configuration newConfig)
{
    base.OnConfigurationChanged(newConfig);

    var nightMode = (newConfig.UiMode & UiMode.NightMask) == UiMode.NightYes;
    // Swap your resource dictionary here
}
```

**TL;DR:** `StaticResource` → `DynamicResource` for runtime updates; add `ConfigChanges.UiMode` to prevent the activity restart.
